---
import Frame from '../components/PageFrame.astro';
import { products } from '../data/site';
const items = [
  {
    title: 'Plain-language choice finder',
    body: 'Choose the problem closest to yours and see a reasoned suggestion for which local demo to explore.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Comparable feature table',
    body: 'Compare purpose, input, interaction and limitations using the same criteria.',
  },
  {
    title: 'No purchase implication',
    body: 'There are no subscriptions or pricing tiers. Every recommendation leads to a fictional product demonstration.',
  },
];
---

<Frame label="Compare" items={items}>
  <section class="container section split-section" id="finder">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">A USEFUL FIRST STEP</p>
      <h2>What needs to become clearer?</h2>
      <p>
        The examples serve different questions. Choose the nearest situation,
        read the reason and follow the matching demo. This is a local guide, not
        a software quotation or business assessment.
      </p>
      <p>
        If your needs span all three, start with the{' '}
        <a href="/platform/">platform story</a> and follow the sample request
        through each perspective.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="finder" data-compare>
      <h3>Find your starting point</h3>
      <fieldset>
        <legend>Choose your main challenge</legend>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="challenge" value="process" checked />
          Repeated work with unclear next steps.
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="challenge" value="context" />
          Information that is hard to find.
        </label>
        <label>
          <input type="radio" name="challenge" value="insight" />
          Numbers that need a useful perspective.
        </label>
      </fieldset>
      <div class="finder-result" role="status">
        <h3 data-compare-title>Start with Workflows.</h3>
        <p data-compare-body>
          Make the stages and owners visible, then pause at a deliberate human
          approval gate before hand-off.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" data-compare-link href="/products/workflows/">
          Try Workflows →
        </a>
      </div>
      <button class="text-button js-only" data-compare-reset>
        Reset choice
      </button>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">SAME CRITERIA, DIFFERENT ROLES</p>
      <h2>Compare the examples.</h2>
      <p>
        On a small screen, scroll the table horizontally. Each product page also
        explains its purpose in a single column.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div
      class="table-wrap"
      role="region"
      aria-label="Product comparison, scroll horizontally"
      tabindex="0"
    >
      <table>
        <caption>Fictional PROWORKS demos — no plans or pricing</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Question</th>
            {products.map((p) => (
              <th scope="col">
                <a href={p.link}>{p.name}</a>
              </th>
            ))}
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Best starting point</th>
            <td>A repeatable process</td>
            <td>A source you need to find</td>
            <td>A pattern you need to inspect</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Prepared input</th>
            <td>One sample onboarding request</td>
            <td>Six sample documents</td>
            <td>Three period datasets</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Working interaction</th>
            <td>Progress, approve, complete, reset</td>
            <td>Search, filter, open sources, reset</td>
            <td>Change period, read chart and table, reset</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Human role</th>
            <td>Approve the proposed hand-off</td>
            <td>Assess relevance and source</td>
            <td>Interpret counts and their limits</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Important boundary</th>
            <td>No external execution</td>
            <td>No uploads or live AI</td>
            <td>No real operational feed</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container section reading">
    <h2>Choose a question before choosing a tool.</h2>
    <p>
      A missing process cannot be fixed by adding a chart. A searchable library
      cannot decide whether a request should be approved. Use the examples to
      explore the interface pattern, then consider what your actual team needs.
    </p>
    <p>
      For genuine website design and development, the real creator is ISMAIL.
      PROWORKS has no account creation or sales process.
    </p>
  </section>
</Frame>
